**P4.** The interim is acceptable if the comment and the changelog say so. After the repair the device honours LBA while bit 9 stays clear. ATA-2 says a host shall not issue LBA unless bit 9 is set, and that bit 9 set makes words 60�?"61 valid (S12, READ at 1849�?"1851 and 2871�?"2873). Words 60�?"61 are already nonzero while bit 9 is clear (432�?"442, READ). Leave them. Do not zero them in this round.

**7.1.** The split on bit 6 is right, and non-media opcodes do not compute an address (only `WDCC_READ` / `READMULTI` / `WRITE` / `WRITEMULTI` call the two functions, 973 and 982, READ). Two cells need a different statement. Every LBA with head �%� 1 is undefined in the `int` product, not merely �?oright if the disk is large�??. Past-end LBA stays a zero-filled read and a refused write, with no error bit, which is the CHS behaviour today (S8). The SDH observable stays byte-exact; the composition expression does not.

**Q1(b).** Use (ii). No new field.

```c
d->lba        = (idata >> 6) & 1;
d->drive      = (idata >> 4) & 1;
d->head       = idata & 0xf;
d->sectorsize = idata & 0xa0;          /* bits 7 and 5, kept for read-back */
odata = d->sectorsize | (d->lba << 6) | (d->drive << 4) | d->head;
```

Those four pieces are disjoint and cover the byte, so every `idata` in `0..255` reads back as itself. (i) also works and needs no new field. (iii) is an addition (R13) with a smaller mechanism already available. V17 is what you get from changing only line 2015: `0xb3` reads back `0x93`, `0xe5` still reads `0xe5`, `0x4c` reads `0x6c`. The existing `sdh rb` row does not see it. `sdh rb2` does. N4 sees `0x6c` and also V16 (`0x4c` forced to `0xec`). V17�?Ts predicted delta is not the licence; the witness already requires the byte to round-trip, and N4 has to be measured with the fix. Update the debug lines at 2010�?"2012 and 2018�?"2020 so they stop calling the preserved bits a size. `sectorsize` keeps a reader under (ii). Do not delete the field this round.

