### Q3 - word 49 first; then shape, home, witness term and records

**(a) Word 49**  
- [READ] S10/S17/S22: word 49 is 0 and deliberately pinned; S18: only one battery rig reaches `dev_wdc.c`, with an all-zero disk behind an overlay.  
- [REASONED] Keep word 49 = 0 this round. No measured delta or transferred warrant supports advertising now; R13 bars "it cannot hurt".  
- [REASONED] If advertised now, the only battery rig would see no observable content change, because the disk is all zeros; only IDENTIFY bytes would change. Words 60-61 already carry capacity (S9), so advertising would make them consistent with S12, but that is not a battery-observable delta.  
- [REASONED] The follow-up gate cannot be the five-rig boot battery (S18). It needs a measured delta on a guest that honours word 49 and issues LBA when advertised, or a transferred warrant. File as follow-up.

**(b) Shape and home**  
- [READ] S16/S23/P7: single-leg in gate 10 beside `wdc_altdigin_probe.py` avoids the `wdcaltoffleg` two-leg debt.  
- [REASONED] Adopt the single-leg shape: FIX column against `$PMAX`, result line `N/N passed`, control line `CONTROL=PASS`, denominator pinned by EQUALITY. Gate checks should require `CONTROL=PASS` and non-skip, with the row count pinned by equality.  
- [READ] No dated exemption needed.

**(c) Witness term**  
- [READ] R17(i): requires pre-fix red and post-fix green with the same script. The base leg was measured red before any edit (section 2).  
- [REASONED] Once the fixed leg is green with the same script, the term is `probe:`, not `detector:`.  
- [REASONED] The record must show ORDER: base run timestamp 2026-10-24 17:03 before edit, fixed run after edit with the same script, binary clearance, and that the device-signature control is the sector tags, not the SDH readback (P15).

**(d) Records to touch in the SAME change**  
- [READ] S17: `diff_wdc_identify.c` `row_no_lba_claim()` must be re-authored in the same change.  
- [REASONED] Update it to still pin word 49 = 0, but change the FAIL text because LBA is now implemented while not advertised.  
- [REASONED] Update `gate_offline.sh` pin/comment if the row name or text changes.  
- [REASONED] Update `dev_wdc.c` comment at 374-375 to say LBA is implemented but not advertised.  
- [REASONED] `&& !d->lba` records become accurate after this round; no change required unless they explicitly depend on the old bit-5 meaning.  
- [REASONED] Keep the commit to this round's hunks; coordinate the uncommitted peer hunks in `diff_wdc_identify.c` and `gate_offline.sh`.

**(e) CHANGELOG block**  
- [READ] Must claim: witness; word 49 unchanged; LBA honoured for LBA-mode media commands only; 48-bit commands not implemented.  
- [READ] Must NOT claim guests now use LBA; must not claim coverage of V7, V9, V10 unless rowed.  
- [REASONED] Additionally file: media requests past the image that complete with no error (7.1); the existing words 60-61 nonzero while word 49 = 0 (P4); any record corrections from Q4.

