## Q2 -- the detector

**(a) Cells.** C1-C4, C8, C12, C13, C15, C16, C18: FLOOR, satisfied by witness rows (R1(a) measured READ; clause-(b) halves V1/V14/V17 each predicted red by witness rows -- checked). C5, C10: **FLOOR via R4, not R10** -- `head` is written at the same site as `lba`, so R10's letter exempts it, but the added-conjunct mutant V4 is drawn from a field the guarded body reads, which R4 places in the DEPENDS-ON closure and R3 makes a (d) obligation; the brief's "(d) or (e)" resolves to (d); rows N1/N2 owed. C9: FLOOR via R10 *and* R4 (`sector`/`cyl_lo` written at different register arms than `lba`; V5w/V6w conjuncts); N5 owed. C7: FLOOR via V13w, its only detector; N6 owed (the write site has no CHS row -- the witness's sibling-parity gap is real). C14: FLOOR via V2/V3, separable only at a bits-7/5-clear bit-6-set select; N3 owed. C17: FLOOR via V16/V17; N4 owed. C6/C11: not rowable on this medium (REASONED: cyl � 256  CHS index � 258,047 > 5,040 and LBA � 65,536 > 4,096  both zeros; both writes refused) -- a **recorded blind**, not clause (e) in R6's sense (the mutant V7 *does* distinguish `cyl_hi`; the instrument cannot); discharge by 7.6's disclosure now, N9 filed as the follow-up. C19, C20: NOT A CELL, clause (e) correct (S5: neither expression reads `cur_command`; V19's `drive` is not body-read and drive 1 is refused at 947-954 before any media site). **No missing cell** (R5: no joint cells -- the body branches on nothing, verified from the inlined arm); the missing *disclosures* are: `neg appar` is a harness self-test (its channel is a constant -- R10 vacuous if presented as a device row), and the dead-run vacuous pass of the derived-want rows (below). 7.2(d)'s dominating predicates are complete per the inlined flow (io_enabled 1176, `case wd_sdh`, the MEM_WRITE split); the caller's switch is correctly outside the function boundary (R4).

**(b) Variants.** Checked by enumeration; predictions that verify: V1 (chs s1TAG(1), s2TAG(2), h1(1<<24)+1zeros), V2, V3, V5r (lba 256CHS 1007), V6r (lba 256 *and* lba 0: sum -1  zeros), V8 (N1 serves TAG(5)), V11 (7069, 256255, 0sum -1zeros; wr/wr2 both red on a -1 write), V13, V14 (both halves), V16, V17, V18, V20 -- all as 7.5 states (REASONED). Corrections: (1) **V4r/V4w are (d) floor, not (e)** (above). (2) V18 and V13r under-report (N4 reds under V18 at 0x0c; N6's read-backs red under V13r) -- harmless, more detection, but the table is incomplete. (3) **V15**: at `-O3` without `-fwrapv` expect the 32-bit imul wrap on this target (512�16,777,221 = 2^33+2,560  mod 2^32 = 2,560  sector 5  N1 reds with TAG(5)), but it is UB and not guaranteed; **the source must widen regardless** -- no row on this image distinguishes a widened build from a compiler-widened evaluation, so the widening's licence is S6's UB finding plus the `arcpartlba` precedent, not a detector row. (4) EQUIVALENT in every state: V12 only, and only under S3's census (NOT CHECKABLE). Only-on-this-image: V7, V9 (blind band exactly k � 12: 2^12+5 = 4,101 > 4,096; k = 11 gives 2,053 < 4,096 and N1 reds), V10. V19 is rig-blind (no second disk), not image-blind. **Missing from the tabulated R4 closure:** an operand-*swap* form (R4(2) enumerates swaps among body-read fields; e.g. headcyl shift-swap or sectorcyl_lo -- existing rows red the plausible ones on this image -- lba 256 reds a headcyl swap, lba 70 reds a sectorcyl_lo swap -- but none is tabulated); at the decode line, `>> 4` (reds every lba row) and `& 3` (reds every chs row) -- both caught, neither tabulated.

**(c) Rows.** Every N1-N9 want enumerated correct: N1 (CHS of (h1,s5) = 67  TAG(67) = 0xffbc0043; FIX LBA (1<<24)+5 = 16,777,221 > 5,040  zeros); N2 (read-backs (0xa1,s5)67, (0xa0,s6)5, both valid triples); N3 (TAG(69)/TAG(70)); N4 (0x4c both columns); N5 (triples (0xa4,s5)4+252 = 256 and (0xaf,s63)62+945 = 1007, both valid; HEAD write lands at 1007, FIX at 256; TAG(256) = 0xfeff0100, TAG(1007) = 0xfc1003ef); N6 (write at 9 via (0xa0,s10); TAG(10) = 0xfff5000a); N7 (indices unchanged: (0xa1,s8)70, (0xa1,s7)69); N8; N9 (HEAD: CHS cyl 256 = 258,047 > any ~66,528 capacity  zeros; FIX: LBA 65,536 in file -- and the tag aliasing premise is right: TAG(65536) = 0xffff0000 = TAG(0), so the widened tag is a genuine precondition). Every row's channel varies under its named variant (R10) -- checked per row. **P12's zero-row guard:** N1/N2's wants are literals, so a dead session (got = None) *reds* them (None ? literal) -- the dead run cannot pass them; the in-session tagged companion in N1 is the right second belt (it kills a "FIX serves zeros universally" false-green); generalize: every zeros-wanting row keeps a nonzero-wanting row in its session. **P10: adopt N7** (valid triples; wants unchanged; the witness record stands as measured with the old triples). **P11: adopt N8** (S8 predicts zeros, section 2 measured 0x00000000; strictly stronger than `nehead`, which passes any wrong-but-nonzero value). **P13: adopt N4.** **P14: adopt N3** -- owed by the decode's truth table over the select byte (0x40 is the only corner separating V2/V3), not by driver behavior. **P16: disclose this round, file N9** (and the 8 GiB sparse `<<24` pin as disproportionate); the brief's aliasing arithmetic is correct.

**(d) Null medium and dead run.** Medium: a **non-emulator executable** (R2's letter; an absent binary is converted by `need_exec` into a whole-gate SKIP, S16). Record form: **measure** -- `(c): measured at <artifact>`; the by-construction form is available to the gate (EQUALITY pin + a named dead-run-red row) but the two-leg witness should measure. The predicted 3/19 HEAD, 2/19 FIX, CONTROL=FAIL, exit 1 is **consistent with the inlined mechanics** (REASONED: HEAD passers = chs h1 (want `TAG(S) if S else None`  None == None), lba 256 (HEAD want `hs`  None), neg appar; FIX loses lba 256 because its want TAG(256) is a literal; all other wants literal  red) -- but it rests on (i) the wants in the omitted lines 489-503 being literals (**NOT CHECKABLE** from the packet; S24's citations imply only two derived wants, but the lines are cut) and (ii) the driver surviving, which **S24 itself contradicts** for an immediately-exiting medium: `Emu.send()` has no `OSError` handling, so the likely outcome is an uncaught crash, no sentinel, no score. Both outcomes are possible; which occurs is a property of the medium. Fix `send()` (in-round detector-material repair, R16 L1), then measure and record which outcome the chosen medium gives; the gate reds either way (exit status / missing sentinel). A `None` want **should fail its row**: literal-want rows already do; extending `row_ok` to fail `None` costs nothing on a live run and closes the chs-h1/lba-256 vacuity (dead-run score would drop to 1/19, 1/19). Keep the count-based CONTROL (it is not `all([])` -- R22's warning does not apply). `neg appar`: keep, but label it in the contract as a harness self-test (it catches a mode-ignoring comparator, nothing else; it can never red and must not be counted as device coverage).

**(e) Contract and anchor.** 7.6 corrections: add **V20** (statement order at the write site) to CATCHES; "conditioned on head, cyl_lo or sector" should say `cyl` (both halves -- the cyl_hi half is the disclosed blind); add the swap-form disclosure; add the `neg appar` self-test label and the dead-run/CONTROL disclosure; V15's line should say N1 reds only on a wrapping build. The BLIND list is otherwise correct (V7/V9/V10 both-out enumerated; C19/C20; 48-bit; debug text). **The anchor claim "all five lba rows" is wrong for a +1 shift** (REASONED, enumerated): a -1 shift reds all five (lba 7069, 256255, 0sum -1zeros, write69 reds both wr and wr2); a **+1 shift reds four -- `lba wr2` passes**, because its channel is a CHS read of index 69 and the write moved to 71, which no row reads. If every WRITE moved: `lba wr` reds for any in-file shift (its want is the payload at 70); `lba wr2` adds only the -1 side; N5 reds �1 (255/257 ? 256); N2 is blind to �1 (out-of-file either way, both writes refused); N6 unaffected. The write-site anchor is therefore `lba wr` + N5, and the honest contract text is "-1: five rows; +1: four."

