34: ### Q1(b) The Decode and Read-Back (`D5, P2, R13`)
35: 
36: - **Evaluation of mechanisms `(i)-(iv)` (`READ`)**:
37:   - Look at [`case wd_sdh:`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_wdc.c#L2006-L2022) (`READ`):
38:     - At `HEAD`, `(d->sectorsize << 6) + (d->lba << 5) + (d->drive << 4) + d->head` is byte-exact for all 256 values `0x00..0xff` **only** because `d->sectorsize` holds bits `7..6` and `d->lba` holds bit `5` (`S1`).
39:     - Once `d->lba = (idata >> 6) & 1;`, leaving the read-back formula untouched (`V17`) drops bit 5 on write and duplicates bit 6 into bit 5 on read-back (`0xb3 -> 0x93`, `0x4c -> 0x6c`).
40:   - **Best mechanism: `(ii)` (repurpose `d->sectorsize` in-place to hold the non-decoded bits 7 and 5, `idata & 0xa0`)**:
41:     - On write (`MEM_WRITE`):
42:       - `d->sectorsize = idata & 0xa0;` (or keep the 2-bit value `((idata >> 6) & 2) | ((idata >> 5) & 1)` if a 2-bit integer is preferred, though `idata & 0xa0` is direct)
43:       - `d->lba = (idata >> 6) & 1;`
44:       - `d->drive = (idata >> 4) & 1;`
45:       - `d->head = idata & 0xf;`
46:     - On read (`MEM_READ`):
47:       - `odata = (d->sectorsize & 0xa0) | (d->lba << 6) | (d->drive << 4) | d->head;`
48:   - **Why `(ii)` beats `(i)`, `(iii)`, and `(iv)` (`R13`)**:
49:     1. **Zero struct changes**: Unlike `(iii)`, it adds no field to [`struct wdc_data`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_wdc.c#L106-L154) and removes no field (`P2`, `R13`).
50:     2. **Orthogonal partition of the 8 bits**: `{7, 5}` (`d->sectorsize`), `{6}` (`d->lba << 6`), `{4}` (`d->drive << 4`), and `{3..0}` (`d->head`) are disjoint bit masks whose union is `0xff`.
51:     3. **Byte-exact across all 256 inputs (`0x00..0xff`)**: Kills `V16` (which fails `N4`: `0x4c -> 0xec`), `V17` (which fails `sdh rb2`: `0xb3 -> 0x93` and `N4`: `0x4c -> 0x6c`), and `V18` (which fails `sdh rb`: `0xe5 -> 0xa5` and `N4`: `0x4c -> 0x0c`).
52:     4. **Compatibility with `R13`**: Preserving byte-exact SDH read-back is not an uninvited feature addition-`HEAD` *already* has byte-exact SDH read-back (`S1`), so breaking it (`V17`) would be a regression introduced by this round's own edit.
53:     5. **Debug lines (`2010-2012, 2018-2020`)**: Update the `debug()` format in `case wd_sdh:` to print `lba=%i` (or `sdh=0x%02x, lba=%i, drive=%i, head=%i`) so trace output matches the decoded bit.
