57: ### Q1(c) The Arithmetic and the Two Sites (`D2, D3, P8, R11`)
58: 
59: 1. **64-bit widening is mandatory in this round (`D2`, `P8`, `S3`, `S6`, `V15`) (`READ`)**:
60:    - In [`wdc__read()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_wdc.c#L472-L474) and [`wdc__write()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_wdc.c#L564-L566), `d->head & 0xf` is bits `27..24` of the LBA28 sector number.
61:    - Multiplying by `512` (`<< 9`) places `d->head & 0xf` at bits **`36..33`** of the byte offset.
62:    - In 32-bit `int`, bits `36..33` **do not exist**: for **every** `d->head != 0` (`1..15`), `512 * (((d->head & 0xf) << 24) + (cyl << 8) + d->sector)` overflows 32-bit signed `int` (undefined behavior in C) and, in 32-bit two's-complement arithmetic, shifts `(d->head & 0xf)` completely out of the 32-bit word (`((head & 0xf) << 33) & 0xffffffff == 0`)!
63:    - Worse still, for `head = 1, cyl = 0, sector = 5` (`N1`, `N2`), 32-bit wrap yields `offset = 2560` (sector 5), which **bypasses `#416`'s bounds check** in [`diskimage__internal_access()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/disk/diskimage.c#L1591-L1601) (`S8`) and silently reads or overwrites sector 5 of the 4,096-sector disk!
64:    - Therefore, both sites **must** widen the product to 64 bits in this round, matching the `(int64_t)` idiom already used on the CHS line immediately above them ([`dev_wdc.c:466-468, 559-561`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_wdc.c#L466-L468)):
65:      `offset = (int64_t)512 * (((d->head & 0xf) << 24) + (cyl << 8) + d->sector);`
66:    - Keeping the two inline `if (d->lba)` blocks (rather than refactoring `wdc__read`/`wdc__write` into a helper) preserves the local structure of both functions and matches the 4-site floor accounting (`7.2(b)`, `V14`).
67: 
68: 2. **The `printf` calls (`475, 567`; `D3`) (`READ`)**:
69:    - The `printf("LBA offset = %lli\n", (long long)offset);` lines inside `#if 0` ([`dev_wdc.c:475, 567`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_wdc.c#L475)) **must not** be enabled as `printf`: they would spam host `stdout` on every LBA sector read/write and corrupt console output in `drive_guest.py` / `Emu` sessions. Delete them (or convert them to `debug()`; note [`wdc_command()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_wdc.c#L970-L981) already logs every READ/WRITE command via `debug()`).
70: 
71: 3. **Control-flow trace (`R11`, `S7`, `8.3`, `8.4`, `8.8`) (`READ`)**:
72:    - **`wdc__read(struct wdc_data *d, int count)` ([`dev_wdc.c:459-549`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_wdc.c#L459-L549))**:
73:      1. Computes `int cyl = (d->cyl_hi << 8) + d->cyl_lo;` (`:465`) and initializes `uint64_t offset` to the CHS byte offset (`:466-468`).
74:      2. With `if (d->lba)` enabled (`:472-474`), `offset` is overwritten with `(int64_t)512 * (((d->head & 0xf) << 24) + (cyl << 8) + d->sector)`, which lies in `[0, (2^28 - 1) * 512] = [0, 0x1fffffff00]` (always non-negative when passed as `off_t` / `int64_t` to `diskimage_access`).
75:      3. Enters `while (count > 0)` (`:478`), enforces the `#484` ring occupancy cap (`:514-528`), calls `diskimage_access(d->cpu->machine, d->drive, DISKIMAGE_IDE, 0, offset, buf, 512 * to_read)` (`:531-533`), pushes big-endian 16-bit halfwords into `d->read_buf` via `wdc_put_in_read_buf(d, ...)` (`:501-505`), increments `offset += 512 * to_read` (`:544`), and sets `d->int_assert = 1` (`:548`).
76:    - **`wdc__write(struct wdc_data *d, int count)` ([`dev_wdc.c:555-575`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_wdc.c#L555-L575)) and write drain ([`dev_wdc.c:1846-1880`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_wdc.c#L1846-L1880))**:
77:      1. Computes `cyl` (`:558`), initializes `offset` to CHS (`:559-561`), and with `if (d->lba)` enabled (`:564-566`), overwrites `offset` with the 64-bit LBA28 byte offset **before** `d->write_offset = offset;` (`:572`).
78:      2. Arms `d->write_in_progress = d->cur_command;` (`:570`), `d->write_count = count;` (`:571`), `d->write_buf_p = 0;` (`:573`), `d->status |= WDCS_DRQ;` (`:574`).
79:      3. As the guest stores 512 bytes (or `512 * write_count` for `WDCC_WRITEMULTI`) to `wd_data`, [`DEVICE_ACCESS(wdc)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_wdc.c#L1864-L1879) calls `diskimage_access(..., 1, d->write_offset, b, 512 * count)` (`:1868-1870`), advances `d->write_offset += 512 * count` (`:1873`), asserts the interrupt (`:1875`), and clears `write_in_progress` when `write_count == 0` (`:1877-1878`).
80:    - No control-flow, ring-cap (`#484`), or write-drain (`#478/#479`) invariant is disturbed.
