83: 
84: ### Q1(d) The Option Set (`R12, P18`)
85: 
86: - **Member of the `R12` option set**: **Member 7 (`IMPLEMENT`)** (and **Member 4 (`ACCEPT`)** for bit 6 of `wd_sdh`). Under `R12`, options 1-6 (`CLAMP`, `MASK`, `IGNORE`, `ACCEPT`, `FAULT`, `DECLINE`) must not be chosen by reflex when the unimplemented path is a small, bounded calculation that the file already sketched under `#if 0`.
87: - **Why `FAULT` (`R12` member 5) is not appropriate and what `DECLINE` looks like here (`P18`, `READ`)**:
88:   - Architectural bus fault (`return 0` from `DEVICE_ACCESS(wdc)`, which raises `EXCEPTION_DBE` on MIPS, as documented in the `#494`/`#495` comments at [`dev_wdc.c:750-757, 1547-1553`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_wdc.c#L750-L757)) is **not** how ATA controllers report command errors and would crash or wedge a guest kernel in an unrecoverable bus-error trap.
89:   - Controller-level command refusal in `dev_wdc.c` is `DECLINE` (`R12` member 6 / `P18(b)`): setting `d->error |= WDCE_ABRT; d->int_assert = 1;` and returning without setting `WDCS_DRQ`, as the no-disk check ([`dev_wdc.c:947-954`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_wdc.c#L947-L954)), ATAPI `WDCC_IDENTIFY` ([`dev_wdc.c:955-962`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_wdc.c#L955-L962)), `SET_FEATURES` default (`:1000`), `WDCC_SEC_*` (`:1110`), and `default:` (`:1155`) do (`READ`).
90: - **Why honouring LBA (`P18(a)`) beats aborting with `WDCE_ABRT` (`P18(b)`)**:
91:   1. ATA-2 (`S12`, section 9.1 lines 1850-1851) states *"A host shall not attempt to use LBA addressing unless the device indicates the mode is supported"*; it does **not** require a device to abort bit-6 commands when word 49 bit 9 is 0 (especially when words 60-61 are already non-zero, `S10`).
92:   2. Real guests that issue LBA commands without checking word 49 bit 9 (e.g. FreeBSD `ata`/`ada`, `1.5`, and Linux `ide-disk` via `lba_capacity_is_ok()`, `S23`) work when LBA28 is honoured (`P18(a)`) and fail if aborted (`P18(b)`), whereas CHS guests (`NetBSD`, `OpenBSD`) leave bit 6 clear and never enter the `if (d->lba)` arm.
93:   3. `P18`'s four-option list `(a)-(d)` is complete for command-level dispositions.
94: 
95: ---

