54: WITNESS vs DETECTOR -- THE LINE, AND WHY IT IS NOT SYNTACTIC.
55: 
56:     A DETECTOR asserts the REPAIRED property: it is GREEN once the defect is gone.
57:     A WITNESS   asserts the PRE-FIX SYMPTOM:  it is RED   once the defect is gone.
58: 
59: That is sharp, but no grep can evaluate it.  MEASURED, so this is not a preference:
60: 
61:   * pit8253_latch_probe.py opens "Rung-3 cold-debugger WITNESS for pitlatch / pitclobber"
62:     -- and its rows assert the FIXED behaviour ("R1/R2 fail on the PRE-FIX build"), so by the
63:     line above it is a DETECTOR.  A self-label grep classifies it wrongly and, worse, then
64:     stops asking for a gate.
65:   * hpcmips_ctor_probe.py and sh4_bsc_width_probe.py are DETECTORS whose docstrings both say
66:     "The pre-fix WITNESS ... asserts the SYMPTOM" in prose.  A self-label grep classifies
67:     BOTH as witnesses -- and would then demand they never be gated, which is backwards.
68: 
69: So the class is DECLARED here, by a human, one line each.  The file's own summary line is
70: cross-checked as an ADVISORY (SELFLABEL), never as a failure, for the measured reason above.
71: 
72: WHY GATING A WITNESS IS A FAILURE, not merely pointless -- the tooth in the other direction,
73: which the reading seat's recommendation did not name.  A witness goes RED the day its fix
74: lands.  Wiring one into the battery converts a successful repair into a red gate with a
75: bookkeeping cause: the phantom-regression class this project already names, manufactured on
76: purpose.  So witness entries are checked for the ABSENCE of a gate call.
77: 
78: RETROACTIVE IN DOMAIN, GREEN AT INTRODUCTION.  check_boilerplate.py and check_bugfile_sync.py
79: are forward-only BY DATE because retro-failing an archive of hundreds of ledger rows gets the
80: rule switched off, and a disabled rule is worse than no rule.  That argument does not carry
81: here: the domain is a few dozen files in ONE FLAT DIRECTORY, enumerable in full today, and an
82: unwired probe has no date to be forward-only about.  A date cutoff would also grandfather the
83: four files this check exists for, permanently.  So nothing is grandfathered -- and the check is
84: still green on the day it lands, because each existing gap is written down as a DATED
85: EXEMPTION naming the round that owes it.  Debt that expires, not debt that disappears.
86: 
87: DATES ARE VALIDATED, NEVER GUESSED.  gate_offline.sh records a malformed exemption date that
88: never expired AND still satisfied the coverage check ("ieee_store:2026-8-1", 19 days past,
89: sorted as FUTURE).  Here a missing or malformed date is RED and names itself; it is never
90: silently treated as unexpired.
91: 
92: WHAT THIS CANNOT DO, said plainly so a green line is not read as more than it is:
93:   * it cannot tell whether a gated probe's rows are any good.  gate_offline's selfmutant lane
94:     and the vacuity taxonomy are what answer that; this answers only "does anything run it".
95:   * it cannot stop a DETECTOR being misfiled as tool to silence the requirement.  The
96:     filename tooth below refuses *_probe.py/*_witness.py in that class, which closes the
97:     cheapest form; a rename defeats it.  What is left is a written lie in a tracked file, and
98:     that is the same footing every manifest in this harness stands on.  Said, not hidden.
99: 
100: *** --selftest IS PART OF THE CHECK, NOT A CONVENIENCE. ***  A gate that cannot be shown to
101: go RED is the vacuity class this project names first, and "I ran the mutants once" is a
102: remembered grep -- the mrwstore2 shape, where a round's witness left no artefact and a later
103: row had to re-cost the work.  `--selftest` applies 22 mutants to COPIES in a temp directory
104: (never the repo) and asserts the exit status of each.  It is re-runnable by someone who was
105: not there, which is the only kind of measurement that survives.
106: 
